1
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,860
Hmm, I see, I see.

2
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:22,160
Senpai, who are you talking to?
There's nobody here.

3
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:24,090
Brace yourself for this.

4
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:28,340
I'm possessed by the
spirit of a shogi master.

5
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:30,220
Really?

6
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:36,880
Eek, there really is something here, lady.

7
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:39,900
Mm.

8
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,360
Eek.

9
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:42,320
Eek.

10
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:45,120
You're so easily hypnotized.

11
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:47,400
Take that, a big flying chariot capture!

12
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:48,720
Again.

13
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,680
Senpai, wait, let me take back that move.

14
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,600
I suppose I could wait for you.

15
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,180
The loser becomes the winner.

16
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:58,240
Can I change the menu you're treating me to?

17
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,580
Honda-kun.

18
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:02,000
Fine, as long as you'll treat me again.

19
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,380
Then I'm switching from katsudon to unadon.

20
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:05,620
So that's settled.

21
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:07,420
Sure.

22
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,140
Take back the gold move and I'll let it go.

23
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:17,400
That's a terrible move, but I'll count it as a fair one.
How kind I am.

24
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:24,520
Kichi's lost Hey, don't move that lemon!

25
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,260
On top of that, why am I the one losing?
It's a double pawn!

26
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:31,800
You're right!

27
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:37,300
How careless of me to
make a double pawn foul.

28
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:40,160
Placing two pawns on the
same file is a forbidden move.

29
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,300
Yes! It's unajū!

30
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,600
It's unadon, not unajū.

31
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:53,620
After treating Honda to lunch,
this is all that's left.

32
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:58,260
Yaima, why did you bring Lemon along?

33
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:02,280
Lemon really wanted to ask a favor of the citrus,
so I just brought him along.

34
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,800
He wants to ask me for a favor.

35
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:09,080
Dad threw his back out,
and the shop is short-staffed.

36
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:12,320
Wait, are you saying I
should take a part-time job?

37
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:14,160
That's right.

38
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:20,120
Oh well,
I can't really say no to Lemon's request.

39
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:22,760
Let me do it.

40
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:33,140
When you watch TV, brighten the room
and sit back from the screen, okay?

41
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:46,300
Anyone who's broke, come to me.

42
00:02:47,140 --> 00:02:51,060
I'm broke too, but don't worry.

43
00:02:51,060 --> 00:03:04,920
Look at the blue sky and white clouds.
Things will work out somehow.

44
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:21,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

45
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:26,500
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

46
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:05,840
Lemon Shioya-san, fully equipped

47
00:04:09,640 --> 00:04:10,360
I'm back.

48
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:12,680
Welcome back, miss.

49
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,520
Ichiro, long time no see.

50
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,140
I'm imposing on you again.

51
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:23,000
Sorry about this, Ichiro.

52
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:26,540
We're short on cash before payday anyway,

53
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,700
so this is a real godsend.

54
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:30,180
And I'll pay you a generous wage.

55
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,760
So you'll work until tomorrow, right?

56
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:36,320
And all the sushi you can eat.

57
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:39,300
I haven't eaten a thing since yesterday.

58
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,540
Sure, sure.

59
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,940
Alright, deal's done!

60
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:04,480
You only trained for a month last year,
but you're really something.

61
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:07,800
Despite your face,
your hands are surprisingly skillful.

62
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:10,080
"Despite your face" was uncalled for.

63
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:13,080
Alright, I guess that'll do for now.

64
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,360
Not bad, I guess.

65
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:19,340
Lemon's
"not bad" is high praise, you know...

66
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:21,380
Well then, I'll dig in.

67
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:26,700
Barto, what's the big idea all of a sudden?

68
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:29,080
Having him work part-time is fine

69
00:05:29,360 --> 00:05:31,900
Why on earth do I have
to let you eat my sushi?

70
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:40,280
By contract,
we're allowed to eat all the sushi we want.

71
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,920
H-hey, what do you think you're doing?

72
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:48,800
Everyone, Kankichi is a Ryotsu man!

73
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,160
You mustn't hold back.

74
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:55,160
They're bound to run off as
soon as they've eaten their fill.

75
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:00,060
Granny, Lemon's totally broke.

76
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:01,700
I don't think that's the case.

77
00:06:02,260 --> 00:06:07,980
Naive! If he's a Ryotsu man, he might eat his
fill of our sushi and still make it to payday.

78
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:10,940
Do I look like a bear before hibernation?

79
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:13,240
Don't lump me in with him.
That's an insult to bears.

80
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:17,560
Worse than an animal *sigh*

81
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:24,920
Grandma, that's going too far. Kankichi was
brought here at Lemon's request, you know.

82
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:31,160
Since Lemon brought him, there's no helping it.
So he can eat all he wants, right?

83
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:39,820
You said it, it's settled! Sushi comes after work.
Only through working is one a true human being!

84
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:41,960
For now, sweep in front of the shop.

85
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:46,300
What kind of answer is that? Do it properly!

86
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,400
Yeah, yeah.

87
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,820
Say "yes" just once.

88
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:50,460
Yes.

89
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:54,500
I wish I could become a human already.

90
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,900
Listen, you two.

91
00:06:56,900 --> 00:07:00,960
I'll say it again: never trust that man,
the regular who's always out drinking.

92
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:03,620
Understood?

93
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,920
That sneeze really rattled my belly.

94
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,860
Bless you.

95
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,180
What is it?

96
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:23,240
Why does Grandma hate
men like Ryotsu so much?

97
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:26,380
Grandma's older brother, a man named Kanbei,

98
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:30,040
was a terrible playboy, and she apparently
suffered a great deal because of him.

99
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:32,560
But that's a problem between siblings,

100
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:35,620
so it has nothing to do with Kankichi,
does it?

101
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,720
As I told you before,

102
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:42,060
he tried to steal the treasure
from the cellar of our storehouse.

103
00:07:42,940 --> 00:07:45,080
That was after Matoi's
marriage proposal fell through,

104
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:47,020
and he did it out of spite, I'd say.

105
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,560
Kankichi isn't as bad a man

106
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:51,540
as Grandma makes him out to be, I think.

107
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,220
Yeah, half of what Grandma says is right,

108
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,980
but he has his good points, you know.

109
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:00,280
N-no, this won't do.

110
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:04,740
At this rate, the grandchildren will be
wrapped around that irresponsible man's finger.

111
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:07,780
We have to do something about it.

112
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:24,060
Yes, yes, just wait a moment, please.

113
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,760
Thanks as always, it's us!

114
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:30,460
Yes. A delivery order, is it?

115
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:36,200
Heh heh, understood. We'll be right there.

116
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:40,860
Mrs. Yoshikawa at Okami Heights,
2-chome: five servings of premium sushi.

117
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:43,040
Two of those without wasabi, coming up!

118
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,320
Could you make the nigiri for
the five in the tatami room soon?

119
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,240
Yah!

120
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:54,740
Time for my entrance!

121
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:02,560
Grandma, why do we have to
dress up in disguise like this?

122
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:06,900
I'll explain the reason later.
Let's follow Lemon.

123
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:12,960
Okame...
when's Okame, when's Okame, when's Okame...

124
00:09:13,480 --> 00:09:14,400
That's it.

125
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:18,260
Hah, I'm so hungry.

126
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:23,100
There's nobody here, is there?

127
00:09:31,534 --> 00:09:38,040
so it's four tekkamaki per serving?

128
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:41,700
Nobody would notice if you ate one of each

129
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:46,080
You there, the salt!

130
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:50,600
Not caring about the shop's reputation,
he just tries to fill his own belly.

131
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,620
That man's just that kind of man, Emon.

132
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:57,700
The wasabi really packs a kick.

133
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,640
W-what is it?

134
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,380
I don't know what it is,
but there's too much!

135
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,880
What's wrong, Ishino?

136
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:17,200
Weren't you supposed to
be delivering the orders?

137
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:20,100
The order was five
portions of premium sushi,

138
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,400
and two portions should have
been made without wasabi.

139
00:10:22,400 --> 00:10:24,340
They all have wasabi in them!

140
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:25,460
Oh no.

141
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:27,200
I mixed it up with the
upstairs room's order.

142
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:29,000
Get your act together.

143
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,620
If I hadn't double-checked,

144
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,000
the shop's reputation
would have been ruined.

145
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,340
Sorry.

146
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:36,020
I'll remake them right away.

147
00:10:39,740 --> 00:10:41,100
Typical Kankichi.

148
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,299
No! Don't be fooled!

149
00:10:43,349 --> 00:10:46,140
I only noticed because I happened to
catch it when I was sneaking a bite!

150
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:46,960
Hmph...

151
00:10:48,060 --> 00:10:51,060
As before!
Please set the trays out by the entrance!

152
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:54,400
Ow...

153
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:59,060
The delivery's done,
so why isn't he heading back to the shop?

154
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:02,760
That man! He's obviously slacking off!
Let's follow him!

155
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:43,620
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

156
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:50,720
Rope and duct tape.

157
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,220
Yes.

158
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:53,500
What do you think you're doing?

159
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:56,860
There, now you're all matching

160
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:57,660
Police!

161
00:11:57,660 --> 00:11:58,640
I won't do it again.

162
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,420
Thank you very much.

163
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,240
I don't know how to thank you.

164
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,880
Don't mention it.

165
00:12:09,880 --> 00:12:11,120
It's all part of the job.

166
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:14,532
Let's see, duct tape is 285 yen,

167
00:12:14,582 --> 00:12:18,540
rope is 288 yen, and magazines are 580 yen.

168
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:22,200
That's 1,210 yen including consumption tax,
thank you.

169
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,960
You're going to charge us?

170
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,840
Yes, it's business.

171
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:29,720
Heh, just put it on Chief
Ohara's tab in Katsushika.

172
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,720
Understood, then please sign here.

173
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,240
Are you really going to do this, Kankichi?

174
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:35,976
No,

175
00:12:36,026 --> 00:12:39,120
why does it have to slip
out today of all days?

176
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:43,000
Ahahahaha!

177
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:48,580
Kankichi!
Bring 10 more cans from the storeroom.

178
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:49,140
Coming!

179
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:54,980
Ten cans of beer, coming right up!

180
00:12:58,720 --> 00:13:00,680
Miss, have another drink!

181
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,040
As for me,

182
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:06,020
Hey, mister, this one's not twenty yet,
so she can't drink.

183
00:13:06,020 --> 00:13:07,100
Sorry.

184
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:08,380
That's a shame.

185
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:12,840
Mm, if it's from you, sir,
I'll accept your pour. Okay?

186
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,020
Come on, go on!

187
00:13:16,020 --> 00:13:18,680
Whaaaat?

188
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:24,300
That's good! Hits the empty stomach!

189
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:28,100
Nice drinking, big brother!
You'd better use a glass

190
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,780
Sorry about that.

191
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,780
Here, here, miss, come on, one more cup!

192
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:41,100
I'm feeling great, little old me!

193
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:43,600
Kankichi, you're getting too carried away!

194
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:48,160
What are you talking about? This handsome
customer is the next good one at this!

195
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,820
I like you! Drink up, drink up!

196
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,220
Please call me Ichiro.

197
00:13:55,220 --> 00:13:56,400
Mariners

198
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,060
Come on, Ichiro-kun!

199
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,420
Next one!

200
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,700
That idiot.

201
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:07,240
Doesn't he have any sense of restraint?

202
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:09,620
This is what a real man is!

203
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:12,720
If it's free, he turns into a
sieve and drinks until the very end.

204
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:15,960
Leading off,
Ichiro steps up to the batter's box!

205
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,740
Hit a ball with that thing and it'll break,
you know.

206
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,180
Break?

207
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:24,480
Y-yeah, that's right.

208
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:28,580
If you're going to play baseball,

209
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:32,560
do it like this, all right?

210
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,880
Out!

211
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,020
Safe!

212
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,900
Yoi, yoi, yoi!

213
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:39,620
You could say a person's true
nature always shows in the end.

214
00:14:39,620 --> 00:14:41,220
You understand now, don't you?

215
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,600
This vulgar, good-for-nothing man

216
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:45,280
is Lemon's true colors.

217
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:48,940
Thank you very much.

218
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:51,040
Please come again.

219
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:54,460
Wow, tonight was really fun.

220
00:14:54,460 --> 00:14:56,180
Ichiro, you're the best.

221
00:14:56,180 --> 00:14:59,780
I'll definitely use this
place for our next party too.

222
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:01,200
Th-thank you.

223
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,900
Get home safely.

224
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:06,960
Winning over a customer's heart in one night,
as expected of Lemon.

225
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,660
How did it come to this?

226
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:38,700
Anman-kishi!

227
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:42,780
Ow Why does my head hurt so much?

228
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:45,180
Of course it does, after drinking like that!

229
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,020
You'll be stocking up on trouble!
Get up already!

230
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:50,520
All right, I get it,
so don't shout like that!

231
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:55,720
My head hurts... At times like this,
a hair of the dog is the best cure.

232
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,660
Don't let me sleep!
Are you trying to drink the shop dry?

233
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:00,220
My head!

234
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:03,500
She's a hard-driving old hag!

235
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,360
Who's a hard-driving one?

236
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:13,760
Ugh, that Tagugebaruto
guy really smacked me one.

237
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:15,740
It's Tā-san's graduation ceremony.

238
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:19,700
What happened to you, Lemon?

239
00:16:21,820 --> 00:16:23,380
Hey.

240
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,280
Kankichi, you don't know about Lemon?

241
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:36,440
Everything's arranged with Shioya-san. Dad said his back's much better,
so he was going to attend.

242
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,100
I see, so that's why.

243
00:16:41,780 --> 00:16:44,280
Alright, I'll go in his place.

244
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,120
Kankichi's coming in his place?

245
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,420
Would you rather I didn't?

246
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:51,000
No.

247
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:55,520
Then go home and get ready for kindergarten.

248
00:16:55,520 --> 00:16:56,140
Yeah.

249
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:58,800
Alright, come on.

250
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:01,080
Yah!

251
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,200
Lemon scores 10 points!

252
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:08,020
Kankichi,
you're going to attend as the father?

253
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:11,640
That's fine, isn't it?
Besides, he's happy about it.

254
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:22,780
Can't be helped. Just don't you dare embarrass Lemon, Kankichi.
What's that supposed to mean, Lemon?

255
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:23,500
Pff

256
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,060
What is this?

257
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:32,720
Mm, it's a... lion, right? Well done.

258
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:37,720
Okay, next picture. What is this?

259
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:42,160
Yes, Ma-chan.

260
00:17:43,620 --> 00:17:44,960
Yes, it's Mr. Elephant.

261
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,740
Yes, well done.

262
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,960
Next one is this

263
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:55,100
It's "hippopotamus"

264
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:57,620
Yes, correct!

265
00:17:57,620 --> 00:18:00,340
A hippo is
"hippopotamus" in English, right, George-kun?

266
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:02,840
It's "cat"

267
00:18:02,840 --> 00:18:03,980
How cute, isn't it?

268
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,380
Pig, pig, piggy

269
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:07,900
Yes, correct!

270
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:09,960
You're all such good kids

271
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,060
Next is

272
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:17,140
I'm Ichiro,
standing in as Lemon Gibōshi's father.

273
00:18:18,440 --> 00:18:18,780
Yes.

274
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:20,760
Ichiro-san, what is it?

275
00:18:21,360 --> 00:18:24,060
The first one to raise his hand is Lemon,
isn't he?

276
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:26,320
Why aren't you letting Lemon answer?

277
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,100
K-Kankichi...

278
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,980
I-I'm sorry.

279
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:33,340
Okay, next one. Can anyone answer?

280
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,220
What's wrong, Lemon? Raise your hand.

281
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:41,920
Well, there's no help for it.
Does anyone know?

282
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:43,820
Hippo?

283
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:45,760
Yes, it's already "crow."

284
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:51,440
Well, this is perfect. That brat's dad loves horse racing,
doesn't he?

285
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:53,560
I'd love to see the dad's face.

286
00:18:54,220 --> 00:18:55,780
It's me. Is there something?

287
00:18:57,460 --> 00:18:58,640
Ahahaha!

288
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:00,660
Quiet, please.

289
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:01,780
Hiroshi-kun.

290
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:03,680
It's not Mr. Ōma's name!

291
00:19:03,680 --> 00:19:05,220
Mr. Ōma is fine.

292
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:07,600
Well, this is the last one.

293
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,960
Who knows this one?

294
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,740
Th-then...

295
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:13,340
Do you know, Lemon?

296
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:17,080
It's called the Alexandra
Trivania Swallowtail,

297
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,620
a rare swallowtail butterfly.

298
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:20,520
I see.

299
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,680
That's right, a perfect answer!

300
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,240
So, what's Lemon's answer?

301
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:31,040
I'm not your dad! Saying
"chicken karaage in a katsu sando" like that, you bastard, that's not something people can easily say!

302
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:32,860
Y-yeah, that's right.

303
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:35,700
That uncle is funny!

304
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:37,020
Uncle Hera!

305
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:42,080
Hey! Aren't you from Jukokudo!

306
00:19:42,380 --> 00:19:43,760
Ryo-san!

307
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:47,220
Your kid goes to this kindergarten?

308
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:50,340
Yeah, but why are you here, Ryo-san?

309
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:52,720
I'm standing in as the father, a stand-in.

310
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:56,900
Wow, so flashy!
That guy's Akira's dad, right?

311
00:19:57,500 --> 00:20:00,200
Akira's dad in front of all these people.

312
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:06,980
Akira...

313
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:11,220
Don't make fun of people
for their clothes or looks.

314
00:20:11,220 --> 00:20:13,320
I'm sorry.

315
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:15,620
Alright, got it?

316
00:20:16,360 --> 00:20:19,120
Jukokudo performs as comedians in Asakusa.

317
00:20:19,120 --> 00:20:21,060
That's their uniform, so to speak.

318
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:29,660
Is that so? Wow, clothes are part of the craft, though.
Akira, your dad has a proper job.

319
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:33,340
You should be proud too yeah.

320
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:34,420
Stand-in Daddy is cool!

321
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:45,940
Ryo-san, I was wrong too. I rushed over right after my stage show,
so this is how I'm dressed. See? Not a bad dad

322
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:46,300
Yeah.

323
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:49,780
Sensei, sorry for interrupting your class.

324
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:53,560
No, it was a different kind of lesson,
but we learned a lot.

325
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:54,600
Hey, everyone.

326
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:55,980
Yes!

327
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:01,940
That's right. Since Akira's dad does stage shows,
it's a perfect chance.

328
00:21:01,940 --> 00:21:04,600
Since it's perfect timing,
let's have him show us his ventriloquism.

329
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:05,360
Yes!

330
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:09,940
No, but I didn't bring a puppet.

331
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:13,340
Alright, then I'll be the puppet myself.

332
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:16,180
Yeah.

333
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:21,360
Ryo-san, we're starting.

334
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:22,620
Yeah, okay.

335
00:21:24,140 --> 00:21:27,860
Ryo-san, it won't be cheating
if you talk on your own.

336
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:30,180
Right. Let's start over.

337
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,720
Well then, Ryo-san, shall we begin?

338
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:35,400
Yeah, mister.

339
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:37,320
"Mister" is a bit much, Ryo-san.

340
00:21:37,320 --> 00:21:39,760
Right, sorry, mister.

341
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:44,260
Anyway, do you know what my job is?

342
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:45,320
Yeah, I know.

343
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:46,820
You're a ventriloquist, right?

344
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:47,620
Liar.

345
00:21:47,980 --> 00:21:49,040
I'm not lying.

346
00:21:49,040 --> 00:21:51,380
Okay. Do you know what my job is?

347
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,480
I know. You're a police officer.

348
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,120
Wrong.

349
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:57,260
But the Ryo-san I know

350
00:21:57,260 --> 00:21:57,800
Yeah.

351
00:21:57,800 --> 00:21:59,800
is a police officer at the police box.

352
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:00,600
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

353
00:22:00,600 --> 00:22:01,840
Wrong?

354
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:04,320
Wrong. His real job is playboy.

355
00:22:05,460 --> 00:22:07,300
What does a playboy's job involve?

356
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:09,780
Then I'll only tell you, mister.

357
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:10,540
Thank you.

358
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:12,880
First, I go to the
police box in the morning.

359
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:13,720
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

360
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:14,860
Then I sleep until noon.

361
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:16,700
What if the Chief comes?

362
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:17,780
What if the Chief comes?

363
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:18,640
I run away!

364
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:19,600
R-run away?

365
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,480
Swinging on the swings in the park, right!

366
00:22:21,740 --> 00:22:22,400
Swings?

367
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:23,680
Pachinko sometimes!

368
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:24,360
Pow!

369
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:26,180
Come home in the evening, eat, and sleep!

370
00:22:26,340 --> 00:22:28,260
Haha, when do they ever work?

371
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:29,680
So they go out to play!

372
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:31,060
Hey, wait a minute!

373
00:22:31,300 --> 00:22:33,100
Mom, that's about me, isn't it!

374
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:34,280
Busted?

375
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:36,740
I told you to knock it off!

376
00:22:49,380 --> 00:22:50,500
Welcome back, Lemon.

377
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:52,840
How was the parents' observation day?

378
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:56,680
Kankichi didn't make you look bad, did he?

379
00:22:57,180 --> 00:23:00,180
Never mind that, Kankichi was cool!

380
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:03,040
Not that much.

381
00:23:03,700 --> 00:23:06,200
What, Kankichi's cool?

382
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:09,020
Well then, Kankichi, see you later.

383
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:11,700
Yeah, go tell Dad.

384
00:23:13,780 --> 00:23:14,780
That's right, Matoi.

385
00:23:14,780 --> 00:23:18,280
If Matoi doesn't want Kankichi,

386
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,640
then Lemon can be my bride, I don't mind.

387
00:23:22,340 --> 00:23:25,800
W-what? W-w-what do you mean, "what"?

388
00:23:26,360 --> 00:23:27,920
Must-buy!

389
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:50,000
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

390
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:52,940
Lemon! Tell me you're joking!

391
00:23:53,540 --> 00:23:55,840
Kankejaaa!

392
00:23:57,800 --> 00:24:00,820
Fish bait! It's always this!

393
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:27,540
I probably don't want to be
someone who bets foolishly on looks.

394
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:34,460
If you keep letting the road rot at the corner,
the moon slips away.

395
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:42,720
Now isn't everything,
so don't get too reckless about it.

396
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:46,440
Even if you tell a few little
lies and get a bit petty,

397
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:50,600
sometimes you're helping someone.

398
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:53,610
Baby, do you know me?

399
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:54,680
Toward tomorrow.

400
00:24:54,680 --> 00:24:56,880
Nice spirit!

401
00:24:58,160 --> 00:25:01,960
Don't rot, just get things done.

402
00:25:01,960 --> 00:25:04,420
Cute spirit!

403
00:25:04,420 --> 00:25:07,820
What's hard to understand

404
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:11,600
is because I want to look that way.

405
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:17,520
Isn't it better than a
makeover of appearances?

406
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:24,500
Na na na na na na na na na na na na na

407
00:25:29,300 --> 00:25:31,720
Look who's back, Jiri from Hanayama!

408
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:33,460
What the hell are you doing here?

409
00:25:33,460 --> 00:25:36,520
What? A test ride on a magic carpet?

410
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:41,100
You mean like the flying carpet
from Arabian Nights or something?

411
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:44,460
We could make a killing with this thing!

412
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:47,280
Next time: Fly, Magic Carpet!

413
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,340
See you then.

414
00:25:48,340 --> 00:25:50,900
That place has walls.

415
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:54,220
Well, I'm sure it's got walls too.

416
00:25:55,460 --> 00:25:59,420
Come on, everyone, come to our town!

417
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

